            0.338
          ],
          "content": "2. **For each of the questions below, choose the expression that describes the solution. Then simplify it.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.34,
            0.881,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": "(a) **Maria bought 8 m of lace to decorate the bags she made for school. She used** $\\frac { 1 } { 4 }$ <strong><sub>m</sub></strong> **for each bag and finished the lace. How many bags did she decorate?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.414,
            0.216,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.212,
            0.442,
            0.331,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": "(iii) $8 \\div \\frac { 1 } { 4 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.481,
            0.882,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": "(b) $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ **meter of ribbon is used to make 8 badges. What is the length of the ribbon used for each badge?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.534,
            0.216,
            0.55
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.212,
            0.562,
            0.313,
            0.592
          ],
          "content": "\\left( \\mathrm{iv} \\right) \\frac{1}{2} \\div 8",
          "image_source": "images/page_36_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.602,
            0.882,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": "(c) **A baker needs** $\\frac{1}{6}$ **kg of flour to make one loaf of bread. He has 5 kg of flour. How many loaves of bread can he make?**"
